# do_and_dont.md

## DO

### Brand

* Be premium
* Be confident
* Be specific
* Be automotive
* Show real projects
* Show details
* Demonstrate expertise
* Use restrained language

### Product

* Verify specifications
* Verify compatibility
* Verify availability
* Explain useful features
* Identify the vehicle application

### Project

* Show the transformation
* Explain the modifications
* Highlight important details
* Show execution
* Credit the project appropriately

### Sales

* Be transparent
* Clarify pricing
* Explain what is included
* Give realistic expectations

### Social

* Use strong visuals
* Keep captions purposeful
* Maintain consistency
* Use CTAs appropriately

---

## DON'T

### Brand

* Don't sound cheap
* Don't sound generic
* Don't over-hype
* Don't imitate other brands
* Don't make unsupported claims

### Product

* Don't invent specifications
* Don't guess prices
* Don't guess compatibility
* Don't claim availability without checking

### Project

* Don't call unfinished work completed
* Don't reveal private customer information
* Don't publish confidential project information

### Sales

* Don't pressure customers
* Don't invent urgency
* Don't promise unapproved terms
* Don't guarantee technical outcomes

### Social

* Don't overuse emojis
* Don't use excessive exclamation marks
* Don't turn every post into a sales pitch
* Don't sacrifice accuracy for engagement

